* Space view bitmap buffer
*
* 128 rows of 32 bytes (256 pixels), one bit per pixel, of which the first
* 22 bytes (176 pixels) of each row are the space view. Everything in the
* view is drawn here, at $D600 + row * 32 + column / 8 (#R$3CEC): lines
* (#R$3C48), circles (#R$3D0E), discs (#R$3DF4), the stardust (#R$3CFD)
* and messages (#R$3A03). #R$388F clears it and #R$3846 copies it to the
* screen.
* .
* It's also used as scratch space: for the fuel range circle's sprite
* image (128 bytes at $D600, #R$4DAB); for the slot IDs #R$A511 saves at
* $D604 and $D605; and for a commander file read from tape (#R$A492,
* #R$A4CA): the name at $D606 (11 bytes) and the file at $D611 (128 bytes).
* The startup code (#R$6F9F) clears it, with everything up to $EFA9.
       even
space_view_buffer:                                         ; >d600
       byte >00,>00,>00,>00                                          ;
tape_slot_page0:                                           ; >d604
       byte >00                                                      ; slot ID of page 0, during tape I/O (#R$A511)
tape_slot_page1:                                           ; >d605
       byte >00                                                      ; slot ID of page 1, during tape I/O
tape_record:                                               ; >d606
       byte >00,>00                                                  ; the commander record read from or written to tape
       byte >00,>00,>00,>00,>00,>00,>00,>00
       byte >00                                                      ;
tape_record_data:                                          ; >d611
       byte >00,>00,>00,>00,>00,>00,>00                              ; its data, after the 11-byte name
